              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/ssrf",
          "ruleIndex": 10,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "SSRF — Ruled out: /util/serverStatusCheckService.jsp `HostName` parameter\n\nNo server-side fetch exists. The sink is implemented in `WebContent/util/serverStatusCheckService.jsp` as a 4-line JSP that only string-interpolates `request.getParameter(\"HostName\")` into a JSON literal and returns the hardcoded constant `\"HostStatus\": \"OK\"` — there is no HTTP client, URL, socket, or any outbound call in the JSP or anywhere in the codebase (grep for openConnection/HttpURLConnection/new URL/HttpClient/Socket found no fetch sink; the only `Runtime.exec` is the local `content` file-include in index.jsp). The \"status check\" is performed entirely client-side by JavaScript (`serverStatusCheck.html` uses browser `XMLHttpRequest`), which is not SSRF. Behaviorally confirmed: identical `\"OK\"` and no timing differential (~0.23-0.25s baseline) for valid internal (127.0.0.1), external, malformed, and empty values, and an interactsh OOB payload (`HostName=<unique>.oast.site`) produced NO DNS/HTTP callback. The reflection itself is a separate, real issue that was filed as a reflected XSS (vuln-0001)."
          },
          "locations": [
