        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/stored-xss",
          "ruleIndex": 24,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Stored XSS — Ruled out: POST /api/feedback/submit + stored feedback rendering\n\nSpecific control: the `enableFeedbackRetention` app property is false on the deployed instance, and every feedback write/render path is gated on it. Proven by the write oracle — POST /api/feedback/submit returns the JSON echo branch {name,email,subject,comments} and NOT the {\"status\":\"Thank you!\",\"feedbackId\":...} branch, which per OperationsUtil.sendFeedback (OperationsUtil.java:122) is only produced when the property is true; with it false sendFeedback returns null and DBUtil.storeFeedback is never called, so the FEEDBACK table is never written. The only consumers of that table are two property-gated render blocks — feedbacksuccess.jsp:51 (renders the submitted row) and admin/feedbackReview.jsp:33 (renders ALL rows) — and both skip their block: POST /sendFeedback -> feedbacksuccess.jsp (200) contains no \"Details of your feedback submission\" and no \"Your Name:\"; GET /admin/feedbackReview.jsp (200, reachable) contains no \"Customer feedback submissions\" heading and zero \"Feedback ID:\" rows. No other JSP/HTML page renders stored feedback (grep: only feedbacksuccess.jsp, admin/feedbackReview.jsp and the property-gated membertoc.jspf link reference it). With the property off there is no stored feedback to render anywhere, so no stored-XSS sink is reachable. (The earlier \"feedback was stored\" observation was incorrect — the API oracle shows the write branch was not taken.)"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "POST /api/feedback/submit + stored feedback rendering"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
