        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/csrf",
          "ruleIndex": 25,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "CSRF — Ruled out: State-changing web forms (POST /bank/doTransfer, /admin/addUser, /admin/changePassword, /sendFeedback, /doSubscribe, /bank/customize.jsp)\n\nDual finding: forms carry no anti-CSRF tokens and the server ignores Origin/Referer (a POST with forged Origin/Referer executed server-side), BUT the control that applies to a browser is Chromium's SameSite=Lax-by-default: an empirical cross-origin top-level form POST from 127.0.0.1:8899 to demo.testfire.net/admin/addUser omitted JSESSIONID (only the non-auth AltoroAccounts cookie was sent) and received 302 -> /login.jsp, so the action did not execute. GET requests to addUser/changePassword/sendFeedback/doSubscribe return 405; GET /bank/doTransfer returns only the form (no state change observed). Not exploitable in modern browsers."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "State-changing web forms (POST /bank/doTransfer, /admin/addUser, /admin/changePassword, /sendFeedback, /doSubscribe, /bank/customize.jsp)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
